#: includes/class-simple-seo-github-updater.php:103
msgid "Version 0.18.0: the Import tab takes over the settings and the SEO fields of All in One SEO too, and removes what AIOSEO left in the database. Version 0.17.0: the Import tab takes over the settings and the SEO fields of Rank Math too, and removes what Rank Math left in the database. Version 0.16.0: the Import tab also removes what Yoast SEO left in the database once its data is imported, part by part, after a backup is confirmed. Version 0.15.0: the Import tab takes over the settings of Yoast SEO and the SEO fields of posts and terms, leaving Simple SEO's own values as they are. Version 0.14.0: the Yoast SEO post meta themes read and write (_yoast_wpseo_title, _yoast_wpseo_metadesc and the like) is Simple SEO's own fields. Version 0.13.0: the Yoast SEO filters themes hook into (title, description, Open Graph, robots, breadcrumbs, sitemaps) change Simple SEO's output. Version 0.12.0: themes made for Yoast SEO keep working without it: wpseo_replace_vars(), yoast_breadcrumb() and WPSEO_Primary_Term are answered by Simple SEO. Version 0.11.0: llms.txt for AI assistants, built from the pages search engines may show, one for each language under wp-loc. Version 0.10.0: the Clean-up tab removes the WordPress version, shortlink, discovery links, emoji script and feed links from pages, each by its own switch. Version 0.9.0: robots.txt and .htaccess edited on the Files tab, with a history of versions; a .htaccess that takes the site down is put back at once. Version 0.8.0: breadcrumbs for themes (PHP, Twig, shortcode) with their own tab, and the primary category of a post. Version 0.7.0: XML sitemap at the addresses Yoast SEO used, a sitemap for each language under wp-loc. Version 0.6.0: settings for the home page, the 404 page and password-protected content. Version 0.5.0: Open Graph and X card. Version 0.4.0: canonical address, noindex and nofollow. Version 0.3.0: page title and meta description from fields and templates. While another SEO plugin is active, nothing is printed."
msgstr ""

